ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the sibling PowersharePage P7)
  • `TeslaChargingSessionsPage` (View) + `@Observable TeslaChargingSessionsPageModel`
    (state holder; ZERO networking in the view, ADR-004). The model consumes a
    `TeslaChargingSessionsDataSource` seam with one method per ported web hook —
    loadVehicles ↔ useVehicles (GET /vehicles), loadTeslaChargingSessions(vin:) ↔
    useTeslaChargingSessions (GET /tesla/charging/sessions{?vin}), and
    refreshTeslaChargingSessions(vin:) ↔ useRefreshTeslaChargingSessions
    (POST /tesla/charging/sessions/refresh{?vin}). Production injects the shared KMP
    repositories; the page default is a representative local seed (NOT production data).
  • Pure, unit-tested derivations (web inline memos): buildMonthlyCost, the mapPoints
    filter, the client range filter, and the default-range seed live in
    TeslaChargingSessionsModels.swift; the CSV encoder (web exportSelectedCsv) and the
    display formatters live in TeslaChargingSessionsPageModel.swift / *Format.swift.
  • Units: energy is SI watt-hours converted to the user unit at the render boundary via
    the shared engine (Units.formatEnergy / @Environment(\.tsUnits)); peak power is the
    kW API field shown verbatim (web fmtNumber(peak_power_kw,0)+"kW"); duration is SI
    seconds rendered "Xh Ym"; cost/rate use the currency formatter. Nothing non-SI stored.
  • Adaptive macOS(regular)/iOS(compact) via #if os(iOS) horizontalSizeClass → isCompact:
    header reflow, summary grid reflow, DataTable columnar-vs-card (TSDataTable).

