PRE-EXISTING ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION (full disclosure — NOT this change; NOT red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Two PRE-EXISTING, out-of-scope files are UNMODIFIED by this change (verified via
`git status --porcelain`) and outside this artifact's allowed files. They fail identically
on a clean tree under the available Xcode 26.5 / Swift 6 front-end (the repo's macOS
verification is documented PENDING in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md; the sibling
PowersharePage P7 log records the identical isolation):

  1) apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/Input.Previews.swift  (committed ed5f636e3)
     2x "cannot use explicit 'return' statement in the body of result builder 'ViewBuilder'"
     inside its `#Preview` blocks. Confirmed via a clean `xcodebuild build` (no exclusion):
     this was the ONLY file with `error:` diagnostics — i.e. every TeslaChargingSessions*
     file, AppRoute, and TeslaSyncApp compiled cleanly alongside it.
  2) apps/apple/Tests/Unit/Features/Admin/GDPRExportPageModelTests.swift
     pre-existing main-actor-isolation diagnostic (see SleepEfficiency / Powershare P7 logs).

To exercise build+test for THIS page without editing out-of-scope files, both were isolated
via the command-line build setting EXCLUDED_SOURCE_FILE_NAMES (a build override, no source
edits). With them isolated the macOS app target builds clean, this page's 25 tests pass, and
the iOS-Simulator (arm64) app target builds clean. Code signing was disabled
(CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO) because no development certificate exists on this runner — an
environment constraint unrelated to the page. The iOS destination is pinned to arm64
(EXCLUDED_ARCHS=x86_64) because the KMP Shared.xcframework ships ios-arm64-simulator only
(no x86_64 slice) — a framework-packaging constraint, not a code issue. Fixing the two
pre-existing files would breach this artifact's allowed-files scope, so they are untouched.

